The subtraction can overflow for valid int values, which is undefined behavior. Compare the values directly:

```c
static int compare_ints(const void *a, const void *b) {
    int x = *(const int *)a;
    int y = *(const int *)b;
    return (x > y) - (x < y);
}
```

The result is negative, zero or positive without subtracting the input values.

